                <pb facs="0785" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4005: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Vice Consul at Viborg</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Imbrie</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-08T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your No. 3, March 2. Department has no adequate information regarding Russian
                    Whites referred to. This Government not in a position to offer any support or
                    assistance but wishes to be kept advised developments. You are to exercise
                    extreme caution not to encourage false hopes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
